# SparkFun Pro RF - LoRa, 915MHz (SAMD21), and SparkFun boards generally.
#
# PlatformIO's own 99-platformio-udev.rules does NOT cover vendor 1b4f. Checked
# 2026-08-21 against the copy shipping with PlatformIO 6.1.19: zero entries,
# case-insensitive. So installing PlatformIO's file silences its warning and
# leaves this board exposed to the thing the warning is really about.
#
# Without this rule the board enumerates with ID_MM_CANDIDATE=1, which means
# ModemManager will open the port and write AT commands at it to find out
# whether it is a cellular modem. Two consequences on this hardware:
#
#   1. Those bytes arrive at the running sketch. `probe` and `i2c_scan` re-run
#      on ANY keypress, so they will appear to re-run on their own.
#   2. If it happens during an upload, it lands in the middle of bossac's
#      conversation with the SAM-BA bootloader. That failure looks random.
#
# Both the application and the SAM-BA bootloader report 1b4f:214f, so matching
# on the vendor alone covers both states.

ATTRS{idVendor}=="1b4f", MODE:="0666", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1", ENV{ID_MM_PORT_IGNORE}="1"
